      "name": "TrajectoryGraph",
      "signature": "pub struct TrajectoryGraph { pub graph: petgraph::graph::DiGraph<ToolNode, ()>, pub last_node: Option<NodeIndex>, pub total_mutations: usize, pub total_reads: usize }; impl TrajectoryGraph { pub fn new() -> Self; pub fn push_tool(&mut self, node: ToolNode) -> NodeIndex; pub fn detect_circular_loops(&self) -> Vec<CircularLoopAnomaly>; pub fn calculate_efficiency(&self) -> f32; pub fn calculate_monotonicity(&self) -> f32; }",
      "description": "Directed graph representation of agent execution paths built by pushing ToolNodes in turn order; detect_circular_loops runs petgraph's Tarjan SCC to find cyclic tool loops and redundant file exploration.",
      "error_conditions": []
    },
    {
      "name": "compute_grounding_score",
      "signature": "pub fn compute_grounding_score(transcript: &CanonicalTranscript) -> f32",
      "description": "Computes Argument Grounding Score G = (Grounded Tool Args) / (Total Invocations). Returns 1.0 when total_tools == 0 (no division by zero).",
      "error_conditions": ["Returns 1.0 (not NaN/panic) when total_tools == 0."]
    },
    {
      "name": "compute_recovery_index",
      "signature": "pub fn compute_recovery_index(transcript: &CanonicalTranscript) -> f32",
      "description": "Computes the Error Recovery Index R = adaptive_error_pivots / total_error_events, where an adaptive error pivot is an error on turn i followed by no error on turn i+1. Returns 1.0 when total_error_events == 0 (no division by zero).",
      "error_conditions": ["Returns 1.0 (not NaN/panic) when total_error_events == 0."]
    },
    {
      "name": "calculate_monotonicity",
      "signature": "pub fn calculate_monotonicity(transcript: &CanonicalTranscript) -> f32",
      "description": "Convenience helper that builds a TrajectoryGraph from a transcript's tool calls in turn order and computes the monotonicity coefficient M in [0.0, 1.0], measuring whether execution avoided circular exploration loops.",
      "error_conditions": []
    }
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-070",
      "criterion": "WHEN a transcript contains 3 identical CodeSearch invocations sharing the same query (which grounds to target_symbol per ground_tool_intent, lib.rs:196-205) without interleaving mutations, THE SYSTEM SHALL identify a Tarjan SCC cyclic loop and emit a CircularLoopAnomaly.",
      "is_error_case": false,
      "judgment_call": false,
      "reasoning": "Fixed two audit-confirmed defects (2026-08-20): (1) the real emitted type is CircularLoopAnomaly (lib.rs:18, api_surface line 19-23), not \"CycleAnomaly\" -- the wrong name was also independently leaking into SPEC-LUMEN-007-INSIGHTS's FindingGenerator signature, fixed there too. (2) The example was changed from a FileRead-based scenario (3 identical view_file invocations) to a CodeSearch-based one, because detect_circular_loops (lib.rs:88-107) only checks target_symbol for redundancy, never target_file -- confirmed by direct code read. FileRead/FileEdit ground exclusively on target_file (ground_tool_intent, lib.rs:198-199), so a repeated-FileRead cycle as originally worded would NOT actually be detected by current code; the example must use a tool that grounds on target_symbol (CodeSearch) to be a true statement. File-based redundancy detection (repeated reads of the same file) is a real, currently undetected gap -- not fixed here since it requires a lib.rs code change (checking target_symbol.or(target_file) rather than target_symbol alone), out of scope for a specs-only pass; tracked as a follow-up."
