Execute via full TDD cycle (red -> green -> commit). Medium-severity finding from an adversarial review. No plan@1/spec_file_path exists, proceed directly from this brief -- the design is already worked out from reading the real code.

Workspace: /Users/gabe/Projects/lumen. Baseline: 21 fixes landed (cb29996..9b08bbd), `cargo test --workspace` green.

## The bug

`crates/lumen-analysis/src/accumulators/context_growth.rs`: `ContextGrowthAccumulator.previous_prompt_tokens` is a plain `u64` (line 18), defaulting to 0 via `#[derive(Default)]`. The growth-detection guard (line 36):
```rust
if prompt > self.previous_prompt_tokens && self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0 {
```
uses `self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0` to mean "we've seen a real previous turn" -- but this conflates the type's default-zero (genuinely "no previous turn yet") with a REAL previous turn whose prompt_tokens happened to be exactly 0 (a legitimate reading, not absence of data). Concretely: a three-turn sequence with real `prompt_tokens()` values `[500, 0, 5000]` -- after turn 2 (prompt=0), `previous_prompt_tokens` becomes `0`. On turn 3 (prompt=5000), the guard `5000 > 0 && 0 > 0` evaluates the second clause as FALSE, so the real 4500-token-equivalent jump from turn 2 to turn 3 is silently never recorded in `total_growth`/`max_jump_tokens`, even though it's a genuine, large jump. Note the file ALREADY has the correct pattern one field over -- `initial_prompt_tokens: Option<u64>` (line 17) correctly uses `None`/`is_none()` to distinguish "unset" from "real zero" (lines 32-34) -- `previous_prompt_tokens` just never got the same treatment.

## The fix

Change `previous_prompt_tokens: u64` to `previous_prompt_tokens: Option<u64>` (mirroring `initial_prompt_tokens`'s existing correct pattern in the same struct). Update `update()`'s growth-detection logic:
```rust
if let Some(prev) = self.previous_prompt_tokens {
    if prompt > prev {
        let jump = prompt - prev;
        self.total_growth += jump;
        self.max_jump_tokens = self.max_jump_tokens.max(jump);
    }
}
self.previous_prompt_tokens = Some(prompt);
```
(replacing the old combined `if prompt > self.previous_prompt_tokens && self.previous_prompt_tokens > 0 { ... } ... self.previous_prompt_tokens = prompt;` block). This correctly means: on the very first usage-bearing turn, there's no previous value (`None`), so no growth is computed (correct, matches existing first-turn behavior) -- but from the SECOND turn onward, `previous_prompt_tokens` is always `Some(actual_value)`, even if that actual value happens to be 0, so a real zero-to-nonzero jump is no longer silently skipped.

Read the CURRENT exact code first before editing -- confirm line numbers/structure match (the struct/logic shown above should be accurate but confirm before changing).

## TDD steps

1. Write a failing test in crates/lumen-analysis/tests/test_accumulators.rs (add to the existing file, find ContextGrowthAccumulator's existing tests for the established fixture-building pattern): feed three usage-bearing turns with `prompt_tokens()` sequence `[500, 0, 5000]` (construct real `CanonicalTurn`s with `usage: Some(TurnTokenUsage { input_tokens: ..., cache_creation_tokens: 0, cache_read_tokens: 0, output_tokens: ..., reasoning_tokens: 0 })` such that `prompt_tokens()` -- input+cache_creation+cache_read -- equals 500, then 0, then 5000 respectively) -- assert `total_growth`/`max_jump_tokens` in the finalized `ContextGrowthMetrics` correctly reflects the 5000-token jump from turn 2 to turn 3 (i.e. `max_jump_tokens == 5000`, not 0).
2. Confirm red against the current code (the 5000 jump should currently be missing/max_jump_tokens should be 0 or reflect only some other jump, not 5000).
3. Implement the fix.
4. Confirm green: new test passes, full existing test_accumulators.rs suite passes with no regression -- especially the existing ContextGrowthAccumulator tests covering the first-turn case and the missing-usage-turn case (these should behave identically to before, since this fix only changes what happens when a real turn has EXACTLY zero prompt tokens, not the first-turn or no-usage cases).
5. Run `cargo test -p lumen-analysis`, then `cargo test --workspace` to confirm zero regressions.
6. Commit.

Report: test results and confirmation of zero regressions.

